This wheel contains the ArcadeDB engine (https://github.com/ArcadeData/arcadedb, release named in
arcadedb.ENGINE_VERSION) compiled ahead of time with GraalVM Community Edition 25.4.4.1.1 into libarcadedb.so.
The NOTICE file of ArcadeDB (components developed for OrientDB, the openCypher grammar) and the NOTICE files of the bundled Apache
libraries (Lucene, Commons Lang, Micrometer, Swagger) are reproduced verbatim in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

GraalVM native-image runtime and JDK classes in libarcadedb.so
  A native image links the Substrate VM runtime (garbage collector, threads, runtime support) and parts of the OpenJDK class library
  into the library. These parts are licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 WITH the "Classpath" Exception
  (licenses/GraalVM-CE-LICENSE.txt, licenses/GraalVM-native-image-LICENSE.txt, and verbatim in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). The exception lets you link and distribute them with code
  under other licences, and it is why this wheel as a whole stays Apache-2.0 for ArcadeDB's own code. The corresponding source:
    GraalVM:  https://github.com/oracle/graal            (release vm-25.4.4.1.1 line; the build used community-25.4.4.1.1+1.1, whose release file names commit 95ce1499c8c96ab7d5a6697c5b4bf42160f3b68b of substratevm)
    OpenJDK:  https://github.com/openjdk/jdk             (jdk-25 line used by that GraalVM build)
  Other GraalVM modules carry the licences in licenses/GraalVM-THIRD_PARTY_LICENSE.txt (graal-sdk and polyglot: UPL-1.0).
  Oracle GraalVM (GFTC) is not used; only Community Edition.

libjvector-x86_64.so, libjvector-aarch64.so
  The native vector kernels of JVector 4.0.2 (https://github.com/datastax/jvector), Apache-2.0, unmodified, taken from the jvector jar.

Java libraries, the Highway/jvector kernels and JDK data inside libarcadedb.so: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md (generated by gen_notices.py).

System libraries linked dynamically and NOT shipped:
  Linux:   libz.so.1, libm.so.6, libc.so.6, libpthread.so.0, libdl.so.2, librt.so.1 (libarcadedb.so, built in a manylinux_2_28 container);
           libstdc++.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1 (the libjvector libraries only)
  macOS:   the system libraries of macOS
  Windows: the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime (VCRUNTIME140.dll, VCRUNTIME140_1.dll) and the Windows C runtime (api-ms-win-crt-*.dll); CPython itself needs the same files
